# Requirements

## Hardware Requirements
    - 16 GB RAM recommended
    - ~60–80 GB free storage recommended
    - x64 processor with virtualization support

## Software Requirements
    - VirtualBox - Used for VM virtualization 
    ( https://www.virtualbox.org/wiki/Downloads ) 
    - Kali Linux ISO Used as Attack/Testing machine
    (https://www.kali.org/get-kali/kali-installer-images )
    - Windows 10&11 ISO Used as Target/Monitored Endpoint 
    (https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/software-download/windows11)

## Objectives: 
The lab requires two VMs so that one can act as attack/simulation 
machine while other acts as target endpoint.

In this setup : 
- Kali Linux is used to generate controlled security activity,
- Windows acts as the monitored endpoint where security events and
  logs are generated. 

This environment can be used to practice attack simulation, security
monitoring, log analysis, detection, and incident investigation.

## Planned network architecture
 Each VM uses two network adapters:
    - Adapter 1 - NAT (provides internet access for updates, installation and downloading)
    - Adapter 2 - Internal Network : Creates an isolated communication channels between VMs)

